# my-pantry

A small .NET application for managing pantry products.

## Stack
- ASP.NET Core API
- Entity Framework Core
- SQL Server
- Docker Compose

## Solution structure
- MyPantry.Api: REST API and static web UI
- MyPantry.Core: domain models and contracts
- MyPantry.Infrastructure: EF Core DbContext and repository implementation
- MyPantry.Web: MVC sample project

## Run locally
1. Start Docker Desktop.
2. Run `start.bat` from File Explorer or Command Prompt (or `.\start.ps1` from PowerShell). The script builds and starts SQL Server and the API, waits for the API health check, then opens the app in your browser.

To stop the containers, run `docker compose down` from the project folder.

The app is available at http://localhost:8080.

The API endpoints are available at:
- GET /api/products
- POST /api/products
- GET /api/products/{id}
- PUT /api/products/{id}
- DELETE /api/products/{id}
